==Faroese==
[[Image:Stream in gasadalur.jpg|thumb|300px|Dalsá í Gásadali]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ɔaː]|lang=fo}}<ref>{{fo-lit-FA|volume 2, page 2, entry ''á<sup>1, 2</sup>''}}</ref>
* {{rhymes|ɔaː|lang=fo}}

===Etymology 1===
Long Old Norse {{IPAchar|/a/}}. Often written as ''[[ā]]'' or normalized '''á''' or even ''[[aa]]'', compare Swedish, Danish, Norwegian [[å]].<ref>Vibeke Sandersen: „[http://www.dsn.dk/nfs/2002-3.htm Om bogstavet å]“ in ''Nyt fra Sprognævnet'' 2002/3 September.</ref>

====Noun====
{{head|fo|letter|upper case|Á}}

# {{Latn-def|fo|letter|2}}

====See also====
* {{list:Latin script letters/fo}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|fo|non|á||river}}, Svabo: ''Aa'',<ref name=Sv>{{fo-lit-Sv|Aa<sup>1</sup>|1}}</ref> from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*ahwō}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*h₂ekʷeh₂||water}}.

====Noun====
{{fo-noun|f|áar|áir}}

# [[brook]], [[stream]], [[river]]

=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|poetry}} {{ux|fo|'''áir''' [[renna]] [[vakur|vakrar]] [[har]]|the '''rivers''' flow beautiful there|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''áirnar''' [[standa]] á [[svølg]]i|the '''rivers''' stand on deep water|inline=y}} (= it's raining a lot) (compare {{m|fo|áarføri}})
* {{ux|fo|[[um]] '''áir''' [[og]] [[gjógv|gjáir]]|over '''rivers''' and gorges|inline=y}} (= to travel a long way)
* {{ux|fo|fara [[yvir]] um '''á(nna)''' [[eftir]] [[vatn]]i|go over '''the river''' in order to get water|inline=y}} (= to look for unnecessary struggle)
* {{ux|fo|[[tað]] [[gekk]] [[sum]] [[eftir]] '''ánni'''|it went like after the '''river'''|inline=y}} (= it was very easy)
* {{ux|fo|[[ganga]] / [[fara]] [[í]] '''áir'''|go to '''the river''' in order to fish trouts|inline=y}}<ref name=Sv/> (described in ''Føroysk orðabók'' 1998 as local usage in the island of [[Vágar]] about fishing trouts in a lake<ref>{{fo-lit-FO|Entry ''á<sup>2</sup>''}}</ref>)

=====Declension=====
{{fo-decl-noun-f2 (á)|á}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|brook}} {{l|fo|løkur}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|fo|non|á||on, onto, in, at}}. <!-- Svabo: ''aa'' --> <ref name="Sv2">{{fo-lit-Sv|aa<sup>2</sup>|1f.}}</ref>

====Preposition====
{{head|fo|preposition}}

# {{lb|fo|with accusative}} [[on]], [[onto]], [[to]], [[near]], [[beside]]
# {{lb|fo|with accusative|fjords, bays, harbours}} to
# {{lb|fo|with dative}} [[on]], [[in]], [[at]]
# {{lb|fo|with dative|place names}} in
# {{lb|fo|with dative|fjords, bays, harbours}} at, in
# {{lb|fo|with dative|seafaring and fishery}} at

=====Usage notes=====
The preposition 'á' is used with accusative case if the verb shows movement from one place to another, whereas it is used with dative case if the verb shows location. This is the same usage as with German {{m|de|auf}}:
: '''Governing accusative'''
* {{ux|fo|[[leggja|legg]] [[bók]]ina '''á''' [[borð|borðið]]|place the book '''on''' the table|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|[[hann]] [[fara|fer]] [[umborð]] '''á''' [[skip|skipið]]|he goes '''aboard''' the ship|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|[[skriva]] '''á''' [[talva|talvuna]]|to write '''on''' the blackboard|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|[[fara]] '''á''' [[fjall]]|to go '''into''' the mountains|inline=y}}
: ''with fjords, bays, harbours''
* {{ux|fo|skipið [[koma|kom]] '''á''' [[Vestmanna]]|the ship came '''to''' Vestmanna|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|skipið kom '''á''' [[Havn]]ina|the ship came '''to''' Tórshavn|inline=y}}

: '''Governing dative'''
* {{ux|fo|bókin [[liggur]] '''á''' borðinum|the book is '''on''' the table|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|hann er umborð '''á''' skipinum|he is '''aboard''' the ship|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|[[tað]] [[standa|stendur]] '''á''' talvuni|this stands '''on''' the blackboard|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|[[vera]] '''á''' fjalli|to be '''in''' the mountains|inline=y}} (in order to roundup the sheep<ref name="Sv2"/>)
: ''Place names'' (''antonym:'' {{l|fo|av}})
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Eiði]]|'''in''' Eiði|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Glyvrar|Glyvrum]]|'''in''' Glyvrar|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Húsar|Húsum]]|'''in''' Húsar|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Kirkja|Kirkju]]|'''in''' Kirkja|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Skáli|Skála]]|'''in''' Skáli|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[Velbastaður|Velbastað]]|'''in''' Velbastaður|inline=y}}
* {{ux|fo|'''á''' [[bygd]]|'''in''' the village (countryside)|inline=y}}
: ''with fjords, bays, harbours''
* {{ux|fo|skipið lá '''á''' Havnini|the ship lays '''in''' Tórshavn|inline=y}}
: ''with seafaring and fishery''
* {{ux|fo|vera '''á''' [[útróður|útróðri]]|to be fishing (with a rowing boat)|inline=y}}<ref name="Sv2"/>

===Etymology 4===
{{onomatopoeic|fo}}.

====Interjection====
{{head|fo|interjection|head=á!}}

# [[oh]]!
# {{non-gloss definition|animal sound of the puffin ({{l|fo|lundi}})}}
: {{ux|fo|[[lundi]]n [[siga|sigur]] '''á á á'''|the puffin says "oh oh oh"}}

===Etymology 5===
From {{inh|fo|non}}.

====Verb====
{{head|fo|verb}}

# {{inflection of|eiga||archaic|3|pres|lang=fo}}

